# Test authoring

Assert what a user can observe, not how the DOM happens to be built.

- Locate elements by role and accessible name (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`), by text, or by a stable `data-testid`.
  Never by class name, tag nesting, or DOM position.
- Assert observable state: visible text, accessible name, `aria-current`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-expanded`, `aria-disabled`.
- Never assert markup internals: SVG path `d`, `outerHTML`, `innerHTML`, inline `style`, class names, spacing, colors, motion timing.
- To confirm something looks right, take a screenshot.
  Do not string-match markup.
- A test may read a component's source only when its subject is wiring: which command a control invokes, whether a destructive action sits behind a confirmation.
  Name the test for that subject.

## Where a test runs

- `*.test.ts` under `src/main`, `src/contract`, `src/lib/**/platform/` and `*.platform.test.ts`: the `main` vitest project, on Node with real `node:sqlite` and the real filesystem.
- Other `*.test.ts` under `src/lib` and `src/renderer`: the `renderer` project, on Node.
  `$state` works, `$effect` does not run, `mount()` throws.
- `*.browser.test.ts`: the `renderer-browser` project, on jsdom with the client runtime.
  Use it for anything that mounts a component or depends on an effect.
- `tests/e2e/*.spec.ts`: Playwright against the built app (`pnpm --filter malini test:e2e`).
- No vitest project collects `*.spec.ts` under `src/`.
  A file named that way never runs.
- Renderer tests swap the platform with `setPlatformForTest(createFakePlatform(seed))` from `$shared/port`.
  The fake answers every contract command through one `install<Domain>Fake` per domain in `$shared/port/fake/`.
